1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,109
As I said earlier, there is I think at Rexford an excellent combination of physical

2
00:00:06,109 --> 00:00:12,018
and geographical advantages-as well as having a rural setting and still being close to

3
00:00:12,018 --> 00:00:16,845
central London, something that will certainly be of interest to you is that Rexford

4
00:00:16,845 --> 00:00:20,070
is just 35 minutes from London Airport.

5
00:00:20,070 --> 00:00:24,550
At Rexford we have a strong research capability.

6
00:00:24,550 --> 00:00:32,873
We came 7th out of 101 universities in last year's research assessment, carried out by a government body

7
00:00:32,873 --> 00:00:39,230
and did particularly well in your particular subjects, engineering and science.

8
00:00:39,230 --> 00:00:45,133
Actually we got a top research grade of five for engineering, geography

9
00:00:45,133 --> 00:00:46,880
and computer sciences.

10
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:53,454
One further point-and I know from talking to you individually that a number of

11
00:00:53,454 --> 00:00:59,927
you may be looking for some experience in industry after the course-is that all our science

12
00:00:59,927 --> 00:01:06,000
and engineering research departments have unusually close relationship with industry in the area.

13
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:09,271
Anyway that's enough sales talk from me...

14
00:01:09,271 --> 00:01:13,188
I'll just take a sip of this coffee that's just arrived, thank you,

15
00:01:13,188 --> 00:01:17,500
and then I'll say something about what actually happens when you apply.

16
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:17,550
Right...

17
00:01:17,550 --> 00:01:25,191
Now if you do decide to make an application, what you do is send

18
00:01:25,191 --> 00:01:28,780
it directly to me in my department.

19
00:01:28,780 --> 00:01:34,170
I will then immediately send confirmation and the application process begins.

20
00:01:34,170 --> 00:01:34,220
Er...

21
00:01:34,220 --> 00:01:40,114
I'd like to say at this point that you shouldn't worry if this process

22
00:01:40,114 --> 00:01:44,472
doesn't work all that quickly-I mean occasionally there are postal problems,

23
00:01:44,472 --> 00:01:50,020
but most often the hold-up is caused by references-the people you give as referees,

24
00:01:50,020 --> 00:01:53,190
shall we say, take their time to reply.

25
00:01:53,190 --> 00:01:58,000
Anyway, it's absolutely normal for this process to take three to four months.

26
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:01,888
What I do in this period is keep in touch with you

27
00:02:01,888 --> 00:02:04,480
and reassure you that things are moving along.

28
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:09,403
One of the ways we've devised to help you decide about applying as well

29
00:02:09,403 --> 00:02:14,326
as later when you've been accepted.., hopefully.., is to put you in contact with,

30
00:02:14,326 --> 00:02:19,248
if possible, a student from your own country who is at present studying with

31
00:02:19,248 --> 00:02:19,600
us.

32
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:25,178
What you can do is phone them up-we will, of course, liaise between you-and

33
00:02:25,178 --> 00:02:27,170
discuss your concerns with them.

34
00:02:27,170 --> 00:02:33,387
That way you can get an objective opinion of what you can expect if you come to live

35
00:02:33,387 --> 00:02:39,604
and study at Rexford-not only the academic atmosphere but important details like what the leisure facilities are like

36
00:02:39,604 --> 00:02:44,440
and whether the English weather and food are really as awful as everybody says!

37
00:02:44,440 --> 00:02:49,470
If you decide you can face it, the contact can also help you just

38
00:02:49,470 --> 00:02:54,500
before you leave, with tips on what to pack and that sort of thing.

39
00:02:54,500 --> 00:02:58,562
At the moment I think we've got two second-year students

40
00:02:58,562 --> 00:03:01,000
and one postgraduate from this country.

41
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:05,270
Now to move on to the other concerns you expressed earlier.

42
00:03:05,270 --> 00:03:10,507
At a UK university-as I'm sure you know-you will be in an environment where

43
00:03:10,507 --> 00:03:12,377
independent learning is the norm,

44
00:03:12,377 --> 00:03:15,743
which takes most students a while to adjust to,

45
00:03:15,743 --> 00:03:20,606
and at a time when you will be separated from your normal surroundings

46
00:03:20,606 --> 00:03:22,850
and, in most cases, your family.

47
00:03:22,850 --> 00:03:24,940
This can be a difficult time.

48
00:03:24,940 --> 00:03:30,686
But remember that something like 25% of our student body are international students like

49
00:03:30,686 --> 00:03:31,097
yourselves,

50
00:03:31,097 --> 00:03:38,485
and that there are several organisations in the university and city whose main purpose is to offer help

51
00:03:38,485 --> 00:03:43,000
and ensure that your time with us is enjoyable and useful.

52
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:47,550
One or two of you touched on the subject of accommodation earlier.

53
00:03:47,550 --> 00:03:50,790
So I'll just add a few points:

54
00:03:50,790 --> 00:03:57,270
it is the University's policy to give priority in the allocation of residence places

55
00:03:57,270 --> 00:03:58,659
to three categories,

56
00:03:58,659 --> 00:04:00,047
and those are:

57
00:04:00,047 --> 00:04:03,750
visiting students, exchange students and new postgraduate students.

58
00:04:03,750 --> 00:04:05,298
However, demand exceeds supply,

59
00:04:05,298 --> 00:04:10,715
so there is still a need to put your name down early for campus

60
00:04:10,715 --> 00:04:13,810
accommodation, particularly if your family is accompanying you.

61
00:04:13,810 --> 00:04:19,155
This means that the earlier you decide whether you want to study with us...

62
00:04:19,155 --> 00:04:24,118
and so get the procedure moving, the better it will be for everybody.

63
00:04:24,118 --> 00:04:24,500
Yes.

64
00:04:24,500 --> 00:04:28,640
What if you would prefer to live outside the university?

65
00:04:28,640 --> 00:04:33,370
If you're planning to live off-campus, you've got to sort things out even earlier.

66
00:04:33,370 --> 00:04:38,406
As with everything in short supply, the good accommodation gets snapped up months before

67
00:04:38,406 --> 00:04:43,443
the beginning of term-in other words if you're starting in October you need to

68
00:04:43,443 --> 00:04:47,760
be thinking about it in June or at the very latest July.

69
00:04:47,760 --> 00:04:53,086
So you do need to think very carefully about what you need, how much

70
00:04:53,086 --> 00:04:56,130
you can afford to pay, well in advance.

71
00:04:56,130 --> 00:05:00,916
What you can't do is leave it until a few days before the start

72
00:05:00,916 --> 00:05:01,600
of term.

73
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:06,806
The agencies in town are pretty good-it's just a matter of contacting them in

74
00:05:06,806 --> 00:05:07,550
good time.

75
00:05:07,550 --> 00:05:12,950
Of course, we have a full-time accommodation officer available to help all students.

76
00:05:12,950 --> 00:05:18,211
She'll get in touch with you when you're accepted-she's got plenty of contacts in the town

77
00:05:18,211 --> 00:05:21,170
and will deal with the agencies on your behalf.

78
00:05:21,170 --> 00:05:26,140
One or two of you asked me earlier about your level of spoken English.

79
00:05:26,140 --> 00:05:31,067
Obviously most of you have already achieved a lot-I wish I could speak your

80
00:05:31,067 --> 00:05:32,475
language half as well.

81
00:05:32,475 --> 00:05:36,347
Having said that though, I'm afraid the lecturers will make little

82
00:05:36,347 --> 00:05:40,570
or no allowance for the presence of non-native speakers in the audience.

83
00:05:40,570 --> 00:05:45,716
So anything you can do to improve your spoken English-even beyond the pretty high

84
00:05:45,716 --> 00:05:50,862
levels most of you have already reached-will help make your stay with us that

85
00:05:50,862 --> 00:05:52,700
bit more fun for you.

86
00:05:52,700 --> 00:05:58,380
Some extra practice before you arrive is worth more than.., for example private lessons

87
00:05:58,380 --> 00:05:58,786
afterwards,

88
00:05:58,786 --> 00:06:01,220
when you won't really have time.

89
00:06:01,220 --> 00:06:01,605
Oh...

90
00:06:01,605 --> 00:06:05,073
and one last thing before I invite further questions:

91
00:06:05,073 --> 00:06:07,000
it's very important that you...
